    "final_text": "I added a v2.4.0 section to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`. It uses the version from `VERSION`, the date from `RELEASE_DATE`, and the same format as the earlier entries:\n\n```\nv2.4.0 - 2026-10-20\n  * CSV export for the report command (ACME-412)\n  * Retry uploads on HTTP 503 with backoff (ACME-415)\n  * Fix crash when the config file is empty (ACME-419)\n  * Fix wrong totals in the monthly summary for leap years (ACME-423)\n```\n\n- **ACME-421 is left out.** It was the only change marked `!`, meaning it would have broken existing usage (removing the `--legacy` flag from sync). Since it was reverted, `--legacy` still works and this release has no breaking changes. That fits the 2.4.0 version number, since a minor version bump shouldn't break anything.\n- **Contributor names are left out**, because the earlier entries don't include them either. I can add them if you want to credit people.",
